{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"I found a second issue in `gen_ffi`: if a prototype already exists, it assumes it is compatible and then indexes parameter types by the current call’s arity. That explains both LLVM verifier failures and compiler crashes. I’m going to add a source-side compatibility check before using an existing prototype."}}
