{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"agent_message","text":"I noticed one compatibility nuance while reviewing the patch: undeclared non-intrinsic FFI calls are intentionally represented as varargs when they create the prototype, but can also reuse a declared prototype later. I’m adjusting that branch so declared calls are strict, while unchecked calls only need to be safe for the prototype they found."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"agent_message","text":"The safer shape is to distinguish three cases: declared FFI must match the previous prototype exactly, intrinsics must match their exact call shape, and unchecked C FFI can reuse a vararg prototype but otherwise must fit the fixed prototype already present. I’m patching to that behavior."}}
