{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"I’ve found the likely root cause: when a tuple element’s static type is a union but the generated value is still a primitive `Bool` (`i1`), the generic pointer cast path asks `gen_box` to box the union type itself. Unions have no primitive representation, so that path fails internally instead of boxing the concrete `Bool`."}}
