{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_68","type":"agent_message","text":"There’s a more precise source-level bug here: control expressions cast each branch to the phi type using the branch’s own type. If the phi is a union object pointer and a branch is `Bool`, this is fine. The tuple path only fails if it re-casts that already boxed value as a concrete tuple subtype later. I’m going to add a guard against null unbox results in the union-to-tuple path and make it skip non-tuple subtypes defensively."}}
